-> What is O(log n) time complexity? Give an example.

O(log n) means the time reduces exponentially as input grows.
Example: Binary Search (halving input each step).

O(log n) means the algorithm reduces the problem size by half (or a fixed fraction) at each step.
Time increases very slowly on keep increasing the input because we keep dividing the problem
