-> What is Dynamic Programming

It is a Technique for solving Complex Problems, by first breaking into collection of simpler Sub-Problems,
then solving each sub-problems just once, and 
then storing there solutions to avoid Repetetive Computations.

There are 2 Approaches of Dynamic Programming:
Top-Down Approach (Memoization)
Bottom-Up Approach (Tabulation)

Memoization:
It is equal to sum of Recursion and Caching, "Recursion" means calling the function itself and "Caching" means storing the intermediate results.

Tabulation:
It solves the same kind of problems, but it remove the recursion, there is no Stack overflow issue and no overhead of the recursive functions.
