-> What is array, and how it stored in Memory, Advantage and Disadvantage of array?

An array is a data structure that stores a fixed-size sequence of elements of the same data type. It allows random access using an index.
Formula: Address(arr[i]) = Base Address + (i * size of data type)

Suppose: arr[0] is at address 1000
Size of int = 4 bytes
Then: Element Address
arr[0]	1000
arr[1]	1004
arr[2]	1008
arr[3]	1012
arr[4]	1016

Advantage:
Fast access using index (O(1) time complexity)
Efficient memory utilization
Easy to traverse and sort

Disadvantage:
Fixed size (cannot dynamically resize)
Insertion and deletion operations are costly (O(n) in the worst case)
