Jump Search works only for sorted array. Imagine you have a large data set, and you have to find Target;
Linear search will consume alot time and memory, as it compares with every element present in Array

For Jump Search: 
int arr = [2, 3, 5, 22, 34, 56, 78, 90, 123, 125]
int start = 0
int end = root(n) //n is size of array n ~ 3 (as underroot of 10 aprx 3)
target = 34

